      "content": "I am so sorry to hear that therapy hasn't brought relief for your deep sense of loss, and it makes complete sense that you feel this pain is about grieving the disappearance of your very self. When grief feels this identity-disrupting, simple comfort words often fail because the lack of authentic purpose is a profound and unique struggle. Please know that a crisis counselor who specializes in identity grief or trauma might offer a different perspective than standard therapy, as their specific training could help you re-find a way to feel present. You are heard, and the fact that you are describing this vulnerability so clearly shows a significant part of you still wants to understand and heal.",
